  "notes": [
    "**Oír** is highly irregular in all tenses",
    "Present: irregular \"yo\" form (oigo), plus spelling changes for i→y in some forms",
    "Preterite: spelling change i→y in 3rd person (oyó, oyeron), accents on other forms",
    "Imperfect: regular pattern but with accent on \"í\" (oía, oías, etc.)",
    "Used for involuntary hearing (perceiving sound)",
    "Don't confuse with **escuchar** (to listen - actively paying attention)",
    "Common usage: *oír música* (to hear music), *oír un ruido* (to hear a noise)",
    "Related expression: *¡Oye!* (Hey! / Listen!)"
  ],
